<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 99.80 from 99.50, the German finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The move brings the yield on the Series 120 five percent paper to 5.05 percent from 5.12 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
